/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 57 550 [
[(This patch takes a sound, analyzes windows in it both for channel magnitude and)]
[(for phase precession in each channel \050compared to another overlapping window\051. The)]
[(real-time output recreates the same magnitudes and phase precession, although the)]
[(phases themselves are in general different. You can control either the location or)]
[(its motion \050setting location stops motion, while setting a non-zero motion causes)]
[(the location to change automatically\051. "Rewind" goes back to the beginning. You)]
[(can use different window sizes \050use the message boxes - the number box is for)]
[(readout\051. The "lock" feature forces phase coherency between neighboring channels,)]
[(which makes a more present sound but can add artifacts to the sound. Look into the)]
[([pd fft-analysis] subppatch to see the workings.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 57 402 [
[(Note: The algorithm was altered and updated in Pd version 0.44 in a way that)]
[(affected the result.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
